---
code: K0022
title: Empty Match
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, pattern-matching, match]
description: "'match' expression must contain at least one pattern arm"
---

A `match` expression must contain at least one pattern arm (`pattern => expression`). Empty `match target {}` blocks are not permitted.

## Example

This error occurs when a `match` block has no arms inside its braces:

```kura
fn describe(x: Int): String =>
  match x {}
```

## Solution

Add one or more `pattern => expression` arms (including a catch-all `_` arm if needed):

```kura
fn describe(x: Int): String =>
  match x {
    0 => "zero"
    _ => "non-zero"
  }
```
